.page lsblk 1 list block devices

# SYNOPSIS
*lsblk*

# DESCRIPTION
`lsblk` reads `/proc/partitions` and prints a table of the block devices the kernel found: the name (as in `/dev`), the size, whether it is read-only (RO), whether it is a whole disk or a partition (TYPE), its filesystem label, the driver that serves it and the model. If there are no devices it says so.

# EXAMPLES
    lsblk

# SEE ALSO
mount(8), dd(1), lspci(1)
